JDBC in PySpark
What is JDBC?

JDBC stands for:

Java Database Connectivity

It is used to connect PySpark with databases like:

MySQL
SQL Server
Oracle
PostgreSQL
Why JDBC is Used

Using JDBC, Spark can:

Read database tables
Load SQL query results
Write data into databases

jdbc_url = "jdbc:databricks://dbc-9d7ea6b8-7c69.cloud.databricks.com:443/default;transportMode=http;ssl=1;AuthMech=3;httpPath=/sql/1.0/warehouses/2655400fbe49a708;"

access_token = "YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN"

query = "SELECT * FROM samples.bakehouse.sales_franchises LIMIT 100"

df = spark.read \
    .format("jdbc") \
    .option("url", jdbc_url) \
    .option("query", query) \
    .option("user", "token") \
    .option("password", access_token) \
    .option("driver", "com.databricks.client.jdbc.Driver") \
    .load()

display(df)

df = spark.read \
    .format("jdbc") \
    .option("url", jdbc_url) \
    .option("dbtable", "samples.bakehouse.sales_franchises") \
    .option("user", "token") \
    .option("password", access_token) \
    .option("driver", "com.databricks.client.jdbc.Driver") \
    .load()
